# Local dev: SQLite file, zero setup.
# Deploy / cross-device sync: swap in a postgres:// URL (Neon, Supabase, Vercel
# Postgres). The datasource provider follows this URL automatically.
#
# IMPORTANT for any *pooled* Postgres URL (Neon's "-pooler" host, Supabase's
# pgbouncer port): append `pgbouncer=true`. It tells Prisma not to use server-side
# prepared statements, which the pooler caches and reuses across connections.
# Without it, any migration that changes a column's TYPE makes every later query
# fail with `cached plan must not change result type` — and restarting the app
# does not clear it, because the stale plan lives on the pooler, not your process.
#
#   postgresql://user:pass@ep-xxx-pooler.region.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require&pgbouncer=true
DATABASE_URL="file:./dev.db"

# Required for the food-photo estimate. https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=""

# Optional: override the vision model used for photo estimates.
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL="claude-sonnet-4-5"
